   "en": "§ The mishna taught that if «the pilgrimage Festival passed and one did not celebrate» it by sacrificing «a Festival» peace-offering, «he is not obligated» to pay «restitution» for «it. And about this it is stated: “That which is crooked cannot be made straight; and that which is wanting cannot be numbered”» (Ecclesiastes 1:15)."
